body:
S1: The owner, 2026-10-06: "The current Help Center doesn't look at all like the one that was supposed to be implemented, and where are the tickets users submitted?"

**Decision D599. Slot S01. Migration 408 for the two stores in step 2.**

### What is true on `main`

- **`/help` is the old docs site.** Task #103 put a front door on it: a gray left rail listing every guide, every guide rendered in one long scroll, a three-column grid of the manifest's sections, and a "Still stuck?" footer at the very bottom.
- **The approved canvas looks different.** `design/canvases/integrated/Help Center.dc.html` (H1 and H2) has:
  - no left rail;
  - a centred lavender search band;
  - seven task-named areas, with licence badges and the surface each guide belongs to;
  - "Popular this week";
  - a "Still stuck?" card;
  - a page for each guide (H2).
- **Four canvas elements were left out on purpose,** and `help_center_contract.test.mjs` pins them absent:
  - Popular this week, because nothing counts views;
  - "Did this answer it?", because nothing stores the answers;
  - "Where this lives" and "Open the surface", because no guide records its surface;
  - "Applies to" and the persona line, because no guide records its licences.
- **Tickets live at `/help/tickets`.** A member sees their own; an admin sees every member's. From `/help`, the only link is "Open a ticket" in the footer, below the whole corpus. The canvas has no ticket screen.

### The work

1. **Build H1 and H2 to the canvas (S1, now):**
   - the hero band;
   - the area cards, two columns wide, with tinted icons and four guides each, every guide carrying its surface;
   - the "Still stuck?" card;
   - one page per guide, at `/help/<area>/<guide>`, with its breadcrumb, "On this page", Related, and "Open the surface", built from each guide's `related` links;
   - no left rail.

   Every existing `#section/sub` deep link keeps resolving.
2. **Two stores, Worker first, in migration 408:**
   - weekly view counts per guide, with no reader identity, for "Popular this week";
   - yes or no per guide, plus "what was missing" after a no, for "Did this answer it?".

   The contract test changes from "absent" to "backed by a store".
3. **Content:**
   - regroup the corpus into the canvas's seven areas;
   - tag each guide with the licences it applies to, which drives "Applies to" and the badges.
4. **The ticket screens wait on the canvas (`needs-design`).** That covers H1's "Your tickets" card, and H3 to H7: Your tickets, Open a ticket, the ticket, the admin queue, and the admin's ticket. The owner pastes the prompt below into Claude Design. Once the canvas is approved, S1 commits the export under `design/incoming/` and builds it.

Steps 1 to 3 ship as PRs that say `Part of` this issue. The last one, after the canvas, says `Closes`.

### Claude Design prompt

```text
Add support-ticket screens to the StudioOS Help Center canvas, the one with "H1 · Help Center" and "H2 · Help · Article". Keep H1 and H2, and add the screens below to the same file.

Match that canvas exactly: the same 1080-wide frames, and the same white header bar with the "A" tile, "Axal VC" and the HELP label. Its tokens:
- Board #eeedf2, frame #f4f3f7. Cards are #fff, with a 1px #e8e6ee border and a 14px radius; inner dividers are #f0eef5.
- Ink #241f38, body #4a4459, muted #6b6577, faint #a49ead.
- Violet #7c3aed, with links and hover #6d28d9, tint #f4f0fe and edge #ddd0fb.
- Green #047857 on #eefbf5 (edge #a7f3d0). Amber #92400e on #fffdf5 (edge #fcd34d). Red #b91c1c.
- Inter 400 to 800, with headings at 800 and tight tracking. Roboto Mono for labels (10px, uppercase, 0.11em tracking), meta lines and every figure (tabular).
- Pills have a 99px radius and buttons 9px. The primary button is violet; the secondary is white with a hairline border.

Draw each new screen at 1080 wide, plus a 390-wide phone layout.

WHAT THE PLATFORM RECORDS ABOUT A TICKET. Draw only these fields.
- Title and description.
- Type: Task, Bug or Feature.
- Category, one of eight: Fund administration, Contracts, Access & permissions, Licence & seats, Billing, Data & reporting, Onboarding, Other. Older tickets have none; they say "No category".
- Priority: Low, Medium, High or Urgent.
- Status: Open, In progress, Resolved or Closed.
- Submitted by; Assigned to (optional); Created; Last updated.
- Tracker: each ticket is mirrored to an issue on the team's tracker, which gives it a number and a link. The mirror can fail. Then the ticket is saved with no number, and nobody can reply on it until it has one.
- A bug's bounty state, in exactly these words: "Under review"; "Confirmed: being fixed"; "Fixed: [N] credits"; "Fixed: no credits granted"; "Fixed: credits taken back"; "Fixed: credits could not be read"; "Not a bug" (the reason is in the replies); "Duplicate" (the replies name the original). Credits are worth US$1 each and are spent on Perks.
- A feature request's review: "Awaiting review", "Approved", or "Declined" with the reason the Super Admin typed.
- The thread: replies from the support team and from the member, each with the author's name, avatar and time.
- Admins only, the SLA tier from priority: Urgent is P1 (24 h), High is P2 (48 h), Medium and Low are P3 (96 h). HQ edits the hours. Each ticket's age band against its tier: On time, Due soon or Overdue.

CHANGES TO H1 (the Help Center home)
- Below the hero, a "Your tickets" card for a signed-in member:
  - their open tickets, at most three, latest activity first;
  - each row: title, status pill, and the bounty or review chip when there is one;
  - links: "All your tickets →" and "Open a ticket";
  - empty state: "No open tickets";
  - Unreadable state: "Your tickets could not be read", with "Try again". A failed read never shows a zero.
- For an admin, the same card reads "Open tickets across the platform" with a count, and links to the queue (H6).
- "Still stuck?":
  - the primary action becomes "Open a ticket";
  - "Message the team" shows only on plans that include chat;
  - then "Email support" (support@axal.vc);
  - keep "What we can see", linking to the Trust Center;
  - remove "Book a walkthrough": nothing books one;
  - keep the status line and "Status page →".
- Keep everything else on H1 and H2 as it is.

NEW SCREENS

H3 · Help · Your tickets (member)
- Breadcrumb: Help / Your tickets. Title "Your tickets", with an "Open a ticket" button.
- Tabs with counts: Open, In progress, Resolved, Closed, All. Filters: type and category.
- Each row: title, one line of the description, type, category, priority and status pills, the bounty or review chip, and "Updated [date]".
- States: loading; empty ("You have not opened a ticket"); Unreadable.

H4 · Help · Open a ticket
- Fields:
  - Title (required);
  - Type: Task, Bug or Feature, required, with no default;
  - Category (one of the eight);
  - Priority, with a one-line hint under each level;
  - Description.
- While the member types the title: "These guides may answer it", with up to three matching guides from the Help Center search.
- For a bug, one line: "A confirmed bug earns credits when the fix ships."
- After submit, three outcomes:
  - saved and mirrored: "Ticket #[n] opened";
  - saved but not on the tracker yet: "Saved. Replies open once it reaches the tracker", with the reason;
  - a field error.

H5 · Help · Ticket (member detail)
- Breadcrumb: Help / Your tickets / [Ticket title].
- Header: title, then type, category, priority and status pills. Then the description.
- A right column, 250px like H2's rail:
  - Submitted, Last updated and Assigned to;
  - the tracker link;
  - a panel that says, in one sentence, what the bounty or review state means. It shows the credits for a fixed bug, and the reason for a declined feature.
- The thread, then a reply box. Show the box disabled for a ticket not on the tracker yet, with "Replies open once this ticket is on the tracker".
- States: loading, not found, Unreadable.

H6 · Help · All tickets (admin queue)
- Every member's tickets. Columns:
  - Ticket (title and one line);
  - Requester (name, linking to the account);
  - Category;
  - Priority, with its SLA tier (P1, P2, P3);
  - SLA: On time, Due soon or Overdue;
  - Status;
  - Bounty or review;
  - Tracker: #[n], or "Not on the tracker".
- Filters: status, type, category, priority and SLA band, plus a title search.
- Admins only: an amber banner at the top, "[n] saved tickets are not on the tracker", with a "Create missing issues (up to 25)" button.
- States: empty, loading, Unreadable.

H7 · Help · Ticket (admin detail)
- H5's layout, plus:
  - a status changer (Open, In progress, Resolved, Closed);
  - the assignee;
  - the tracker mirror's state and its error;
  - for a feature request, a link to the Super Admin's review queue.

RULES
- Never draw an invented figure. Use placeholders such as [Member name], [Ticket title] and [n].
- A failed read says "Unreadable", never 0 and never an empty list.
- The AI is called Eadwyn. Product copy never says advisor, advice, recommendation or fiduciary.
- Under each new frame, a one-line caption like H1's and H2's, saying what the screen is for.
```


